Other build-time tools (Metrowerks toolchain, wibo, dsd, Ghidra, objdiff) are
obtained separately by the user and are licensed by their own authors.

Runtime hardware values and behavior have been cross-checked against external
reference-emulator sources and hardware documentation. Those source trees are
not bundled. Some differential tests read a separately available public
high-level-emulation source file; they do not require a Nintendo BIOS.

Prior work consulted for research and tooling design (not bundled): the DQIX
community projects at https://github.com/DQIX and the ds-decomp toolchain (dsd)
at https://github.com/AetiasHax/ds-decomp. Their code and materials retain
their respective licenses; this project's MIT License does not cover them.

